  "quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "at Zed, we asked ourselves like how can we let users bring their agent of choice to our tool and enjoy like a nice interface that is unified across all of them",
      "timestamp_sec": 14,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=14s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And so that's why we decided we need some kind of type of protocol uh called agent client protocol, uh which is similar to like MCP or uh LSP.",
      "timestamp_sec": 14,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=14s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's a JSON RPC based protocol. And the idea is basically that uh agents and clients can talk to each other through through a unified interface.",
      "timestamp_sec": 54,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=54s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And we also have a bunch of uh clients at this point up to 40 that uh implement this including open claw for example.",
      "timestamp_sec": 54,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=54s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "here's a very minimal coding agent that just doesn't support ACP, but it's kind of the bare minimum you need to like build a coding agent",
      "timestamp_sec": 102,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=102s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, all it has is really like two tools. One to read a file and one to edit an existing file.",
      "timestamp_sec": 147,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=147s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "that is kind of like the way all agents basically work is the model APIs are stateless",
      "timestamp_sec": 147,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=147s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, now the question is how do we make this thing ACP compatible? And hopefully we can do it in 10 minutes.",
      "timestamp_sec": 221,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=221s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And then you have to at minimum implement these three uh four functions.",
      "timestamp_sec": 259,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=259s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "So, basically every time you start a thread in Zed or in a different editor or client, uh you you call a new session.",
      "timestamp_sec": 302,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=302s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "And then you can send updates kind of like notifications to the client that are not like a usual request response, right?",
      "timestamp_sec": 513,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=513s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "you have to emit like a tool call, like session update of type tool call, and then once once the client knows about it, uh you can emit updates for that",
      "timestamp_sec": 691,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=691s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "But MC uh ACP actually proxies the file system too. Like the client can provide a uh a file system capability",
      "timestamp_sec": 731,
      "talk_slug": "building-an-acp-compatible-agent-live",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsxQICTLF84&t=731s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
